**Calculating the Offset of an Element in an Array**

### Problem Description

Given an array of elements, find the offset of a specific element.

### Solution

#### Template

```c
// Calculate the offset of an element in an array
// Input: array, element
// Output: offset of the element in the array

int calculate_offset(int* array, int element, int size) {
    int offset = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
        if (array[i] == element) {
            return i; // Return the offset of the element
        }
        offset++;
    }
    return -1; // Element not found
}
```

#### Example Use Case

```c
int main() {
    int array[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
    int element = 3;
    int size = sizeof(array) / sizeof(array[0]);

    int offset = calculate_offset(array, element, size);

    if (offset!= -1) {
        printf("Element found at offset %d\n", offset);
    } else {
        printf("Element not found\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

### Note

This code assumes that the input array is sorted. If the array is not sorted, the above code will not work as expected. In a real-world scenario, you would want to use a more efficient algorithm to find the element, such as a binary search.

